<article class="env-lemma" id="074F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/074F">Lemma <span data-tag="074F">11.4.7</span>.</a> Let $A$, $A'$ be two simple $k$-algebras one of which is finite and central over $k$. Then $A \otimes _ k A'$ is simple. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $A'$ is finite and central over $k$. Write $A' = \text{Mat}(n \times n, K')$, see Theorem <a href="/tag/0747" data-tag="0747">11.3.3</a>. Then the center of $K'$ is $k$ and we conclude that $A \otimes _ k K'$ is simple by Lemma <a href="/tag/074C" data-tag="074C">11.4.4</a>. Hence $A \otimes _ k A' = \text{Mat}(n \times n, A \otimes _ k K')$ is simple by Lemma <a href="/tag/074D" data-tag="074D">11.4.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>